<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Blitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1940–1941</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Blitz was the German bombing campaign against British cities from September 1940 to May 1941. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> was bombed on 57 consecutive nights at its start, and ports and industrial centres such as Coventry, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liverpool">Liverpool</a> and Plymouth were heavily hit; more than 40,000 civilians were killed, but the campaign failed to break British morale or war production.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-blitz.jpg" alt="The Blitz" width="320" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: German Air Force photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinkel_He_111_over_Wapping,_East_London.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
